## Summary

Implemented **`HelixPage`** — the native SwiftUI/HIG parity of the web `HelixPage` (`/integrations/helix`) — adaptive across macOS + iOS, and committed it (`a456c659b`, 13 files).

**What was built** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Settings/`):
- `HelixPage.swift` — `HelixPage<Content>` view: Integrations › Helix breadcrumb, header (title + subtitle), settings-gated body; success body embeds the existing `AISettings` surface (web `<PageContainer><AISettings/>`).
- `HelixPage.Projection/Model/Views.swift` — pure `HelixPageProjection`, `@Observable HelixPageModel` binding `useSettings` via a P1/S8 seam with P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, the breadcrumb/header/loading/empty/error subviews, and a catalog-backed string facade.
- `HelixRouteRegistration.swift` — `HelixRoute` value, `/integrations/helix` deep-link resolver, and a `.navigationDestination` modifier wired into `SettingsScene` (real NavigationStack registration).
- `HelixPage.Previews/Tests.swift` — per-state previews + XCTest.
- Wired `TeslaSync/Features` into `project.yml`/`.swiftlint.yml`; added 3 web-parity + 5 chrome keys to `Localizable.xcstrings`; created `apps/parity/apple-ledger.json`.

**Verification (all host-runnable gates green):**
- `swiftlint --strict`: 0 violations · `swiftformat --lint`: 0 · placeholder scan: 0 · `xcodegen`: EXIT=0
- **Isolated `swift build`** (Swift 6 complete concurrency): green · **isolated tests: 16/16 pass**; the 3 web-parity strings proven exact in the catalog.
- Caught & fixed a real Swift 6 concurrency error (`static let LocalizedStringKey` → computed vars).
- **`=== PARITY ===` PARITY_COVERED=5/5** (loading, success, 3 strings) with file+symbol+test evidence. Log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`.

**Honest deferral:** the full-app `xcodebuild build test` is DEFERRED to the P99 gate due to pre-existing, out-of-scope blockers (R1 `DashboardWidgetSize` duplicate symbols in `dashboard-widgets/*`, R2 test-files-in-app-target, R3 macOS signing) — identical to predecessor P4 surface gates, with proof that **zero errors are attributable to HelixPage** (the override full-app compile passes Components + all feature-views and fails only in `dashboard-widgets`).

